From a2b0086623f6942c06fe31443390a86d5276f3cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Origin ledger: find a re-homed card's replacement
 without relying on announced scopes

Answers review 5970563622 (request_changes on 9b74d43886): `_Publications` only looked at gateways whose info row
announced the card's board. A replacement published by a gateway with no info row, or one not announcing that
board, was missed, so a removed owner's verified completion settled the row while the card was running elsewhere.
The base ledger kept that row unknown: a regression.

Fix: for every gateway the replica lists, one read of its task keys through the `(gw, coll, key)` primary key,
which covers the read (no row data), then a keyed read per candidate. Built at most once per projection, only when
a removed owner's row asks. Measured on the MacBook's live ledger and replica, five projections each: installed
87-91 ms, this head 104-113 ms (one outlier at 165 ms); the cost exists only while a removed owner's row does.

Tests: a verified completion is never settled while another gateway publishes the same card running, with that
gateway having no info row, an info row for another board, or one for this board (the binding is dropped in all
three); control: the same completion settles when the third gateway publishes only an unrelated card. The
scope-only test of the previous commit is replaced by these. 22 tests in the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
